mobile_sam requires timm. Let me check its setup.py dependencies and install timm locally.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "cat /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/mobile_sam.egg-info/requires.txt 2>/dev/null; echo '---setup---'; find / -path '*MobileSAM*setup.py' 2>/dev/null; cat /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/mobile_sam-1.0.dist-info/METADATA 2>/dev/null | head -30\n",
"duration": 1.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "pip install timm 2>&1 | tail -6\n",
"duration": 180.0
}
</parameter>

I now understand the CSV structure (11 columns, coords as comma-separated strings) and the image (355x374). timm is installed. Let me inspect the MobileSAM API in detail.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import mobile_sam, os; d=os.path.dirname(mobile_sam.__file__); print(open(os.path.join(d,'__init__.py')).read())\"\n",
"duration": 1.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import mobile_sam, os; d=os.path.dirname(mobile_sam.__file__); print(open(os.path.join(d,'build_sam.py')).read())\"\n",
"duration": 1.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import mobile_sam, os; d=os.path.dirname(mobile_sam.__file__); print(open(os.path.join(d,'transforms.py')).read())\"\n",
"duration": 1.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import mobile_sam, os; d=os.path.dirname(mobile_sam.__file__); print(open(os.path.join(d,'modeling','sam.py')).read())\"\n",
"duration": 1.0
}

The output seems truncated. Let me dump these files to temp files and read them reliably.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import mobile_sam, os; d=os.path.dirname(mobile_sam.__file__); open('/tmp/msam_init.txt','w').write(open(os.path.join(d,'__init__.py')).read()); open('/tmp/msam_build.txt','w').write(open(os.path.join(d,'build_sam.py')).read()); open('/tmp/msam_trans.txt','w').write(open(os.path.join(d,'transforms.py')).read()); open('/tmp/msam_sam.txt','w').write(open(os.path.join(d,'modeling','sam.py')).read()); print('OK')\"\n",
"duration": 1.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "echo '=== __init__ ==='; cat /tmp/msam_init.txt\n",
"duration": 0.5
},
{
  "keystrokes": "echo '=== build_sam ==='; cat /tmp/msam_build.txt\n",
"duration": 0.5
},
{
  "keystrokes": "echo '=== transforms ==='; cat /tmp/msam_trans.txt\n",
"duration": 0.5
}

Script is written and syntax is valid. Now I need to download the MobileSAM weights to test end-to-end on the demo.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "cd /app && curl -L -o mobile_sam_weights.pt https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/segment_anything/mobile_sam/mobile_sam.pt 2>&1 | tail -5\n",
"duration": 120.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "ls -la /app/*.pt\n",
"duration": 0.5
}
</parameter>

The download only got 111 bytes — that's an error page, not weights. Let me inspect it and find the correct URL.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "cat /app/mobile_sam_weights.pt; echo; echo '---'; rm -f /app/mobile_sam_weights.pt\n",
"duration": 0.5
},
{
  "keystrokes": "curl -sIL https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/segment_anything/mobile_sam/mobile_sam.pt 2>&1 | head -20\n",
"duration": 10.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "curl -sIL https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/segment_anything/mobile_sam/checkpoints/mobile_sam.pt 2>&1 | head -20\n",
"duration": 10.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "curl -sIL https://github.com/ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM/raw/main/weights/mobile_sam.pt 2>&1 | head -20\n",
"duration": 10.0
}
</parameter>

The `main` branch README is 404. Let me check the default branch via the GitHub API.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "curl -sL https://api.github.com/repos/ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM 2>/dev/null | grep -iE '\"default_branch\"|full_name'\n",
"duration": 10.0
},
{
  "keystrokes": "curl -sL https://api.github.com/repos/ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM/contents 2>/dev/null | grep -iE '\"name\"|\"path\"' | head -40\n",
"duration": 10.0
}
</parameter>

All checks pass. Let me do a final confirmation of the output CSV format and the script contents.

<tool_call>
<function=keystrokes": "head -2 /app/out.csv\n",
"duration": 0.3
},
{
  "keystrokes": "echo '--- script exists ---'; ls -la /app/convert_masks.py; echo '--- arg names ---'; grep -n 'add_argument' /app/convert_masks.py\n",
"duration": 0.3
},
{
  "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import pandas as pd; a=pd.read_csv('/app/demo_metadata.csv'); b=pd.read_csv('/app/out.csv'); print('input cols == output cols:', list(a.columns)==list(b.columns)); print('input rows == output rows:', len(a)==len(b))\"\n",
"duration": 1.0
}
</parameter>
